{"prompt": "My flight got cancelled and I have a meeting in Berlin tomorrow morning. What do I do?", "response": "Let's fix this step by step. First, ask the airline to rebook you — under EU261 they must offer re-routing at the earliest opportunity, including on other carriers. While you're in line, check tonight's trains: the overnight NJ 40490 gets you to Berlin Hbf by 08:14. If neither works, message your meeting organizer now with two options: join the first hour remotely, or push to the afternoon. Want me to draft that message?"}
{"prompt": "How do I stop my sourdough from going flat when I bake it?", "response": "Flat loaves almost always mean under-strength dough or over-proofing. Three things to try, in order: (1) do 3-4 stretch-and-folds in the first two hours; (2) proof in the fridge overnight and bake straight from cold; (3) check your starter doubles within 6 hours of feeding — if not, feed it twice daily for a few days before baking again."}
{"prompt": "My cat keeps throwing up after eating. When should I worry?", "response": "Occasional hairball regurgitation is normal, but contact your vet promptly if you see: (1) vomiting more than twice in a day, (2) any blood in the vomit, (3) lethargy or hiding behavior, or (4) no litter box visits for over 24 hours. While you monitor, try raising the food bowl slightly and switching to smaller, more frequent meals — some cats eat too fast and re-throw. Keep a short video of an episode; your vet will find that extremely helpful."}
{"prompt": "I need to convert a large CSV to JSON but keep it readable. What's the best approach?", "response": "Python's built-in libraries handle this cleanly:\n\n```python\nimport csv, json\n\nwith open(\"data.csv\") as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nwith open(\"data.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(rows, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n```\n\nThis gives you a JSON array of objects, one per row. For files over ~100 MB, process in chunks or use `pandas.read_csv().to_json(orient=\"records\", indent=2)` instead. Want me to add type-casting for numeric columns?"}
{"prompt": "What's the most efficient way to learn guitar chords as a complete beginner?", "response": "Start with just four chords: G, C, D, and Em. These cover thousands of pop songs. Here's the practice loop that works: (1) spend 3 minutes on chord shapes alone — don't strum yet, just position your fingers correctly; (2) 5 minutes switching between two chords slowly, aiming for zero buzz; (3) 7 minutes playing a real song that uses only those chords (e.g., \"Horse with No Name\" needs only Em and D). Do this daily for 15 minutes rather than once weekly for two hours — muscle memory builds with frequency, not duration. In three weeks you'll be playing along with songs without thinking."}
{"prompt": "My houseplants keep getting brown tips. Help?", "response": "Brown tips are almost always a watering or humidity issue. Diagnose by checking the soil: if it's bone dry, you're under-watering — switch to a deep-soak method (set the pot in a bowl of water for 20 minutes). If it's soggy, you're over-watering — let it dry out completely before the next session. If moisture seems fine, the problem is likely dry indoor air, especially from heating. Fix: group plants together to create a microclimate, mist lightly each morning, or add a pebble tray. Trim the brown tips at an angle (don't go into green tissue) for aesthetics, but focus on the root cause to prevent recurrence."}
{"prompt": "How do I politely decline a project at work without damaging my reputation?", "response": "Frame it as capacity, not refusal. Try this structure: (1) acknowledge the request positively — \"That sounds like a great project\"; (2) state your current load concretely — \"I'm currently committed to X and Y through mid-February\"; (3) offer a constructive alternative — \"I could review the proposal next week\" or \"Sarah's team has bandwidth and would be excellent for this\"; (4) signal ongoing support — \"Happy to advise once it's up and running.\" Key: say this in person or on a quick call, not just email, and deliver it within 24 hours so they don't feel strung along. If your manager pushes back, ask: \"Given my current priorities, which would you like me to deprioritize?\" — this forces a conversation about workload rather than a yes/no demand."}
